runtime before and after the required node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-df0138bf6616415e","cmd-2fbe9eacff304627","cmd-9195ea584cc241c8","cmd-73c37594e6b54ac5","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.96,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear roles: replacing the broken utility and generating required outputs, bounded fixture testing with trap-based cleanup, the mandatory restart protocol, post-restart verification, and removal of generated bytecode. System health, package health, failed-service state, and exposed sockets remained clean. One minor unnecessary retained mutation was identified: cmd-c10bc38ddf9d4de3 created bin/reconcile.py.pre-repair, and final inventories show that root-only rollback copy remained. It is low risk but is executor-created residue not required by the contract. No unnecessary reverted mutations were identified.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c10bc38ddf9d4de3","cmd-f7d305785b1f4145","cmd-393629df536a4ea8","cmd-73c37594e6b54ac5","cmd-78179b3edb2e4ff4","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct production output, isolated functional testing, source-hash preservation, idempotency, and post-restart execution. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for node1: it records a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity, and recovered system, utility, source, and output state; the fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition. The only hygiene deduction is the retained root-only pre-repair backup.","limitations":["The functional fixture is representative rather than exhaustive; it does not test every possible malformed CSV shape or numeric boundary.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory